WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.508 --> 00:00:01.418
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

2
00:00:02.153 --> 00:00:04.360
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> This is for my foodie friends.

3
00:00:04.507 --> 00:00:10.699
In case you thought lettuce was only for salads, here I’m cooking it in some butter with an onion.

4
00:00:11.007 --> 00:00:14.712
Then I add some mushrooms, chicken, fresh tomatoes,

5
00:00:14.712 --> 00:00:17.132
and some other things – not sure yet.

6
00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:22.857
Lettuce is also great in soups, or you can grill it and serve it with blue cheese.

7
00:00:24.448 --> 00:00:25.411
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

8
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.065
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> We didn’t feel like cooking last night, and anyway we didn’t have

9
00:00:30.065 --> 00:00:33.847
any food in the house, so we decided to order some takeaway

10
00:00:33.847 --> 00:00:36.786
salads from our wonderful local pizzeria.

11
00:00:37.134 --> 00:00:40.892
They were all very good, but my favourite was a chicken salad,

12
00:00:41.019 --> 00:00:46.543
a bit like a Caesar salad, with carrots, tomatoes, peppers, lettuce,

13
00:00:46.556 --> 00:00:48.682
and some pieces of fried bread.

14
00:00:50.515 --> 00:00:51.571
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

15
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.894
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Dinner last night at a restaurant in Piccadilly, called NOPI.

16
00:00:57.162 --> 00:01:00.385
We had lots of different sharing plates.

17
00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:07.701
I loved everything, especially this dish called <i>shakshuka</i>, which is North African,

18
00:01:07.861 --> 00:01:14.909
and it’s basically eggs in a tomato sauce, but the mixture of herbs and spices

19
00:01:14.909 --> 00:01:17.584
makes it just fantastic.

20
00:01:17.758 --> 00:01:21.851
And the bread we had to dip in the sauce was wonderful, too.

21
00:01:21.958 --> 00:01:24.071
Go there. Soon.

22
00:01:25.716 --> 00:01:26.572
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

23
00:01:27.602 --> 00:01:29.474
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> OK, this is it!

24
00:01:29.581 --> 00:01:31.146
Our Thanksgiving dinner.

25
00:01:31.266 --> 00:01:37.525
All the usual things, turkey with cranberry sauce, roast potatoes, mashed potatoes,

26
00:01:37.699 --> 00:01:42.256
lots of vegetables, and more…and more…

27
00:01:42.324 --> 00:01:46.908
We thought about going to a restaurant this year, maybe having seafood,

28
00:01:46.994 --> 00:01:51.314
but then we decided, no, we like home-made and traditional,

29
00:01:51.368 --> 00:01:54.190
so we stayed at home and cooked together.

30
00:01:54.711 --> 00:01:56.503
So how was yours?